  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ab02225fbc76494eae24904d1b187fca",
      "statement": "The Vercel callback hard-codes `https://vercel.com/api/login/oauth/token` as the token endpoint passed to `arctic`'s `OAuth2Client.validateAuthorizationCode`, because `arctic` does not ship a Vercel adapter and the library's default token URL would be wrong.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/callback/vercel/route.ts#L26-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8ed659b769f0563f93092b96f40861ae5b010f7ecf84e663b2cd9285d6b6e7cf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/signin/vercel/route.ts#L1-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb6f9dd7f5e9fe4af000128aa268bb72f669518169688e29f3f6d0c2fbda8049:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d7837fb17644d469f09a48b07574aa6",
      "statement": "The Vercel sign-in start route at `POST /api/auth/signin/vercel` is the only OAuth start route that returns the authorize URL as a JSON `{ url }` body rather than issuing a 302, because the PKCE handshake requires a client-driven navigation rather than a server-side redirect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/signin/vercel/route.ts#L1-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb6f9dd7f5e9fe4af000128aa268bb72f669518169688e29f3f6d0c2fbda8049:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/session/redirect-to-sign-in.ts#L1-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36be0ef18a67c318c0b6bc5b4ce607bd30031d0810888c876c605c7f2cbdd71a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d31ce2c00db24021848c34a09f9ec279",
      "statement": "`fetchUser` in `lib/vercel-client/user.ts` tries `https://api.vercel.com/v2/user` first and falls back to `https://vercel.com/api/www/user` when the first returns non-200; the parser also normalizes the two response shapes (bare user vs `{ user }` envelope) so both endpoints work.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/session/create.ts#L11-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bad876f27fed1a84732fa3da4113765eff3a3ce8770a4f78ab19282519efd9d2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/vercel-client/user.ts#L1-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7b37fa07f6a3ae63be37f33a5e45fb7fe05a423d1a3fdf0e22ce7dbe5d55952:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10a9e4de4bc041e0b0116701e7ed0338",
      "statement": "`fetchTeams` in `lib/vercel-client/teams.ts` treats HTTP 403 from `https://api.vercel.com/v2/teams` as an empty array (expected for personal accounts that have not been added to any team) but returns `undefined` for any other non-200 status, which the `/api/vercel/teams` route then surfaces as a 500.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/vercel/teams/route.ts#L1-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a4751d416e5813ee8395a390f49606f19bcb90e52257a5c181f29b58c60b67c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/vercel-client/teams.ts#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6fb6aa040911c95c4ca76d6280a374479d002d835e6c5db87b397c40d59bfa65:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1157238445fb436fac952bb59dd9fa08",
      "statement": "Vercel is always a primary identity and never appears in the `accounts` table: `lib/session/create.ts` stores both the access and refresh tokens (encrypted) on the `users` row via `upsertUser`, and the `accounts.provider` schema enum is hard-coded to `'github'`, so the database itself rejects a Vercel link.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/schema.ts#L258-L283",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3560e0b5be165dddea7997114b6db0cf6ac0fc9714a87d5c7ebd17d960c2c6c7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/session/create.ts#L11-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bad876f27fed1a84732fa3da4113765eff3a3ce8770a4f78ab19282519efd9d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7cf1644a60246eea92b747539308487",
      "statement": "`/api/auth/info` rehydrates a Vercel session on every request by re-running `createSession` with the decrypted token from `getOAuthToken`, then re-encrypts the refreshed `user` block and re-issues the JWE cookie; for GitHub-primary users the route returns the existing session verbatim without re-fetching.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/info/route.ts#L1-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7da4fc0fb284ad2a49259126fac2ca3d69428e7f709f5ebf4c3ae8e87c4684e0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/session/get-oauth-token.ts#L17-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45970c7552fa04403eb15b593cd28aa9df2c4b9736eed8d95c6e9757fcbc9f94:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7a98fe1cd3f4b2dbc4c8e63b82575aa",
      "statement": "The Vercel sign-in start route writes three short-lived (10-min) aux cookies — `vercel_oauth_state`, `vercel_oauth_code_verifier`, and `vercel_oauth_redirect_to` — all `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`, and `Secure` in production, and the callback deletes all three after a successful exchange.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/callback/vercel/route.ts#L9-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:379da53105b3b9a0c491f61faca0d2c12fd75f70389348372c5e38b28d364a7f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/signin/vercel/route.ts#L23-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36f5389823458f2cd9917c970dda72582f6d89c018f48ecb8763aa6f928d65ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f1c873b27f764423a4ec208a4133e50a",
      "statement": "The Vercel callback constructs its 302 `Response` (with `Location: storedRedirectTo`) *before* it calls `createSession`, so that a single round-trip can both set the JWE session cookie and navigate the browser to the post-auth target.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/callback/vercel/route.ts#L43-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c563641c933c39aa40d0c8aca3ec77dff2d391fbf464fd6a079a519f489fad9f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_013f6d34a0fe41c99580902174d12379",
      "statement": "The Vercel authorize URL is built with an empty scopes array (the inline comment says `Vercel uses default scopes`), and `createSession` explicitly passes `scope: undefined` to `upsertUser` so no scope value is persisted on the `users` row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/signin/vercel/route.ts#L15-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96540946d287c8e487318e2709869d0f82e251a4c3ea23554a1381fbd5f2f776:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/session/create.ts#L11-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bad876f27fed1a84732fa3da4113765eff3a3ce8770a4f78ab19282519efd9d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec15838e5beb48aa93a34cd0ca2a6129",
      "statement": "For Vercel sign-ins, `upsertUser` only takes the same-primary-update path (case 1) or the fresh-insert path (case 3); the GitHub reconnect-merge branch (case 2) is gated by `if (provider === 'github')` and is skipped for Vercel, so a single real-world Vercel identity always maps to exactly one `users` row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/users.ts#L15-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b0912c5e6093d5cefa799a5aa4fed375e7034af498048da28a89b5542ccb9ed3:"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
